 "q-130072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st and the $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{10})\\cdot {R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers