mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{13}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:=(-2){R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb4f94e5da3777e586ca00b882ebdf2cfc2e4e9c9b97255de3d994c4699b79b0" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4693.json" "file_sha256" "cae1ed929ab7963fd45e5573559691f6a0b94a13cc3dc2ca0c4edf6a9546df53" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4693.json" "file_sha256" "cae1ed929ab7963fd45e5573559691f6a0b94a13cc3dc2ca0c4edf6a9546df53" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4694.json" "file_sha256" "c66245330d26e4ccb5cdae2c4ea864fac150efbb459ffcb1543059a64057d80b" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4694.json" "file_sha256" "c66245330d26e4ccb5cdae2c4ea864fac150efbb459ffcb1543059a64057d80b" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which elementary row operation could transform the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4695.json" "file_sha256" "c71b1e41799a028658e72182d16e31ab53fc4cba001e355a23e0c0ac265ea8fd" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has been changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nNow, applying the operation $R_2:=R_2+1 \\cdot R_1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4+1\\cdot (-4) & 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation could be done by the operation \n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+1\\cdot R_1\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4695.json" "file_sha256" "c71b1e41799a028658e72182d16e31ab53fc4cba001e355a23e0c0ac265ea8fd" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ which elementary row operation could make $a_{22}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4696.json" "file_sha256" "28425ca8a1e67989e8c1d8a22cdd3be17a8e0bb4cb2c49d51cecbb54c5df1c46" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In the given matrix, we have $a_{22}=5$ and we want to perform an elementary row operation that makes $a_{22}=0.$\n\n- We *cannot* make $a_{22}=0$ by switching two rows, because there are no rows with $0$ as the second entry.\n\n- We *cannot* multiply the second row by $0,$ because we are only allowed to multiply rows by *nonzero* constants.\n\n- However, we *can* add a multiple of another row to the $2$nd row to make $a_{22}=0.$\n\nLooking at the first row, we see that $a_{12}=1.$ If we add $-5$ times this entry to $a_{22},$ we will get $a_{22}=0$ as desired. So, the elementary row operation that we need to use is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1.\n$$\n\nApplying this operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1+(-5)\\cdot 3 & 5+(-5)\\cdot 1 & 6+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -16 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the desired elemetary row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1,\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 -5 R_1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/example-4696.json" "file_sha256" "28425ca8a1e67989e8c1d8a22cdd3be17a8e0bb4cb2c49d51cecbb54c5df1c46" "basis" 1382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-130064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0+(-2)(5) & 4+(-2)(2) & 7+(-2)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(1)(5) & 3+(1)(2) & 0+(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 8 & -9 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1+(3)(9) & -3+(3)(6) & -2+(3)(-7) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28+(-1)(-2) & 15+(-1)(4) & -23+(-1)(-3) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 9 & -11 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 26 & 19 & -26 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 27 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-10248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $5$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1+(3)(2) & 2+(3)(0) & 1+(3)(-1) \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9+(5)(2) & 0+(5)(0) & -4+(5)(-1) \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $N?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2+(-2)(1) & 1+(-2)(-2) & 2+(-2)(1) & 3+(-2)(-1) \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end