 nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b