_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-72763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $S$ into the matrix $T$, where\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that changes the $1$st  row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=(-2){R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $1$st and the $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{10})\\cdot {R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-130087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $U$ into the matrix $V$, where\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 2 & \\,2 & \\,1\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{33}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Of the given options, we consider the row operation    \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 2 & \\,2 & \\,1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 3 & \\,0 & \\,0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{3}:=(-1){R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72857" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{33}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50aed26ef029541e3c6bca4dd3bfce4485a93dd5f658a4efb76b88150a4cd32d"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-72860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given \n$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$,\n which of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{31}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e91097d8e18f339ddd8dac5a808f98b3e723f27a8678f536270996a6199c5"} {"question" "q-20386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd8e9